    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0978" n="966" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg966"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.24/1–2545</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation by the Assistant Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clayton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-25">January 25, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">French Lend Lease</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Russian Lend Lease</hi>—3 C credits</p>
                <p>Secretary Morgenthau<anchor n="2" xml:id="d719-f1"/> said that if we still felt
                    that we should stand on an interest rate of 2⅜% on these credits, he would not
                    further oppose it.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Russian Long-Term Postwar Credit</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Secretary Morgenthau said that he disagreed with the view of the President and
                    the Secretary of State on this subject and felt that we should consider
                    immediately a long-term credit of $10 billion to the Russians at a low rate of
                    interest and not condition it on anything else, and stated that he felt sure
                    this is what we would do in the end.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">illiam</hi>] L. C[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">layton</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d719-f1" n="2" xml:id="d719-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary of the Treasury Morgenthau was accompanied by Harry Dexter White and
                    Josiah E. DuBois, Jr., Assistants.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
